<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spanish America</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spanish America refers to the territories in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> colonised and ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, stretching from present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patagonia">Patagonia</a>. It was a major source of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and other commodities. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> note British commercial interest and rivalry with Spain in the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spanish-america.jpg" alt="Spanish America" width="268" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Jluisrs assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Imperio_Espa%C3%B1ol_America_1800.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
